hed in 1917-03-26. A moderately significant entity in the historical record. Relevant to cause-and-effect analysis.", "newValue": "Chulalongkorn University, established on March 26, 1917, in Bangkok, Thailand, stands as a hallmark of modern higher education in Southeast Asia. Named after King Chulalongkorn (Rama V), who is credited with significant reforms in Thai society and governance, the university embodies a transformative period in Thai history that sought to modernize the nation through education and Western influences. The university's creation came amid a backdrop of national identity formation and modernization efforts, reflecting the broader socio-political landscape of early 20th century Thailand.

